  "explicit_non_claims": [
    "No claim that theoretical path bandwidths sum to achieved application goodput",
    "No claim that gateway failover is simultaneous subflow scheduling",
    "No claim that Multipath QUIC is an RFC until publication is confirmed",
    "No claim that a modelled schedule is an observed transport packet schedule",
    "No claim of SOTA superiority before matched pinned transport runs",
    "No claim of production readiness or network actuation",
    "No claim that deterministic segment traces reproduce ACK clocks, congestion control, retransmission or real radio propagation",
    "No claim that shared-risk-group synthetic loss is a calibrated common-cause failure distribution",
    "No claim that links in distinct failure domains provide independent bottleneck capacity",
    "The v1 scheduler permits only one path per declared capacity group and may underuse real capacity within that group",
    "The v1 disjoint-set rule is conservative and is not a general multi-commodity flow optimizer",
    "For more than two paths, deterministic greedy extension may underuse some globally feasible disjoint path sets",
    "Capacity-domain evidence-envelope validation does not cryptographically authenticate the inventory or prove the declared topology is truthful",
    "The scheduler does not discover hidden shared bottlenecks; field negative controls must challenge declared dependency sets",
    "Capacity-domain confidence ppm is a source-declared evidence grade, not a calibrated statistical probability"
  ],
  "baseline_methodology": {
